### Notes
- The `visit` method uses a `seen` set to avoid calling the callback more than once per `ReactiveContext` across matching prefixes.
- In `remove`, prefixes are collected into `empty_prefixes` and then pruned afterward via `prune_if_empty`, handling garbage collection of the subscription tree.
- The test `mark_dirty_marks_descendants_without_remarking_ancestors` verifies each subscriber (root deep, child deep, leaf shallow) is marked dirty exactly once when `mark_dirty(&[1])` is called.

